[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"MongoDB Query Operators: Comparison, Logical, and Element"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"MongoDB provides a rich set of query operators that allow you to specify criteria for selecting documents from a collection. These operators are categorized into several groups, including comparison, logical, and element operators. This tutorial will cover these three categories with examples."},{"order":3,"type":"heading","text":"Comparison Operators"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Comparison operators allow you to compare a field's value against a specified value. Here are some common comparison operators:"},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"$eq: Matches values that are equal to a specified value."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"$gt: Matches values that are greater than a specified value."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"$gte: Matches values that are greater than or equal to a specified value."},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"$lt: Matches values that are less than a specified value."},{"order":9,"type":"bullet_point","text":"$lte: Matches values that are less than or equal to a specified value."},{"order":10,"type":"bullet_point","text":"$ne: Matches all values that are not equal to a specified value."},{"order":11,"type":"bullet_point","text":"$in: Matches any of the values specified in an array."},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"$nin: Matches none of the values specified in an array."},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"Examples of Comparison Operators"},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"// Find documents where age is equal to 30
db.collection.find( { age: { $eq: 30 } } )

// Find documents where age is greater than 25
db.collection.find( { age: { $gt: 25 } } )

// Find documents where age is less than or equal to 40
db.collection.find( { age: { $lte: 40 } } )

// Find documents where city is not equal to "New York"
db.collection.find( { city: { $ne: "New York" } } )

// Find documents where the value of the 'status' field is either "A" or "D"
db.collection.find( { status: { $in: [ "A", "D" ] } } )"},{"order":15,"type":"heading","text":"Logical Operators"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"Logical operators allow you to create more complex query conditions by combining multiple expressions. Common logical operators include:"},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"$and: Joins query clauses with a logical AND returns all documents that match the conditions of both clauses."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"$or: Joins query clauses with a logical OR returns all documents that match the conditions of either clause."},{"order":19,"type":"bullet_point","text":"$not: Inverts the effect of a query expression and returns documents that do not match the query expression."},{"order":20,"type":"bullet_point","text":"$nor: Joins query clauses with a logical NOR returns all documents that fail to match both clauses."},{"order":21,"type":"subheading","text":"Examples of Logical Operators"},{"order":22,"type":"code","text":"// Find documents where age is greater than 25 AND city is "London"
db.collection.find( { $and: [ { age: { $gt: 25 } }, { city: "London" } ] } )

// Find documents where age is less than 20 OR city is "Paris"
db.collection.find( { $or: [ { age: { $lt: 20 } }, { city: "Paris" } ] } )

// Find documents where the 'name' field does NOT exist
db.collection.find( { name: { $not: { $exists: true } } } )"},{"order":23,"type":"heading","text":"Element Operators"},{"order":24,"type":"paragraph","text":"Element operators check for the existence or type of a field. The most common element operator is:"},{"order":25,"type":"bullet_point","text":"$exists: Matches documents that have the specified field. The $exists operator takes a boolean value. If true, the operator matches documents that contain the field, including documents where the field value is null. If false, the operator matches documents that do not contain the field."},{"order":26,"type":"bullet_point","text":"$type: Selects documents where the value of the field is an instance of the specified BSON type."},{"order":27,"type":"subheading","text":"Examples of Element Operators"},{"order":28,"type":"code","text":"// Find documents that have the 'email' field
db.collection.find( { email: { $exists: true } } )

// Find documents that do not have the 'phone' field
db.collection.find( { phone: { $exists: false } } )

// Find documents where the 'age' field is of type 'double'
db.collection.find( { age: { $type: "double" } } )"},{"order":29,"type":"paragraph","text":"These operators can be combined to create complex and powerful queries in MongoDB. Understanding and utilizing these operators effectively is crucial for efficient data retrieval."}]
